<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section>
  <exercises>
    <heading level="1">Section 4.10 Exercises</heading>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, show that $$F(x)$$ are antiderivatives of $$f(x).$$</paragraph>
    <exercise number="465" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$F(x) = 5x^{3} + 2x^{2} + 3x + 1,f(x) = 15x^{2} + 4x + 3$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$F ′ ( x ) = 15 x 2 + 4 x + 3 F ′ ( x ) = 15 x 2 + 4 x + 3$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="466" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$F(x) = x^{2} + 4x + 1,f(x) = 2x + 4$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="467" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$F(x) = x^{2}e^{x},f(x) = e^{x}\left( {x^{2} + 2x} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$F ′ ( x ) = 2 x e x + x 2 e x F ′ ( x ) = 2 x e x + x 2 e x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="468" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$F(x) = \cos x,f(x) = -\sin x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="469" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$F(x) = e^{x},f(x) = e^{x}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$F ′ ( x ) = e x F ′ ( x ) = e x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, find the general form for the antiderivative of the function.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="470" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = \frac{1}{x^{2}} + x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="471" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = e^{x} - 3x^{2} + \sin x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$F ( x ) = e x - x 3 - cos ( x ) + C F ( x ) = e x - x 3 - cos ( x ) + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="472" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = e^{x} + 3x - x^{2}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="473" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = x - 1 + 4\sin \left( {2x} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$F ( x ) = x 2 2 - x - 2 cos ( 2 x ) + C F ( x ) = x 2 2 - x - 2 cos ( 2 x ) + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, find the general form for the antiderivative $$F(x)$$ of each function $$f(x).$$</paragraph>
    <exercise number="474" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = 5x^{4} + 4x^{5}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="475" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = x + 12x^{2}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$F ( x ) = 1 2 x 2 + 4 x 3 + C F ( x ) = 1 2 x 2 + 4 x 3 + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="476" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{x}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="477" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = \left( \sqrt{x} \right)^{3}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$F ( x ) = 2 5 ( x ) 5 + C F ( x ) = 2 5 ( x ) 5 + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="478" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = x^{1/3} + \left( {2x} \right)^{1/3}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="479" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = \frac{x^{1/3}}{x^{2/3}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$F ( x ) = 3 2 x 2 / 3 + C F ( x ) = 3 2 x 2 / 3 + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="480" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = 2\sin (x) + \sin \left( {2x} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="481" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = \sec^{2}(x) + 1$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$F ( x ) = x + tan ( x ) + C F ( x ) = x + tan ( x ) + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="482" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = \sin x\cos x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="483" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = \sin^{2}(x)\cos (x)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$F ( x ) = 1 3 sin 3 ( x ) + C F ( x ) = 1 3 sin 3 ( x ) + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="484" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = 0$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="485" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = \frac{1}{2}\csc^{2}(x) + \frac{1}{x^{2}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$F ( x ) = - 1 2 cot ( x ) - 1 x + C F ( x ) = - 1 2 cot ( x ) - 1 x + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="486" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = \csc x\cot x + 3x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="487" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = 4\csc x\cot x - \sec x\tan x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$F ( x ) = - sec x - 4 csc x + C F ( x ) = - sec x - 4 csc x + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="488" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = 8\sec x\left( {\sec x - 4\tan x} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="489" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = \frac{1}{2}e^{-4x} + \sin x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$F ( x ) = - 1 8 e -4 x - cos x + C F ( x ) = - 1 8 e -4 x - cos x + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, evaluate the integral.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="490" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{(-1)dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="491" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\sin x dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$- cos x + C - cos x + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="492" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\left( {4x + \sqrt{x}} \right)dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="493" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{3x^{2} + 2}{x^{2}}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$3 x - 2 x + C 3 x - 2 x + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="494" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\left( {\sec x\tan x + 4x} \right)dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="495" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\left( {4\sqrt{x} + \sqrt[4]{x}} \right)dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$8 3 x 3 / 2 + 4 5 x 5 / 4 + C 8 3 x 3 / 2 + 4 5 x 5 / 4 + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="496" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$${\int\left( {x^{-1/3} - x^{2/3}} \right)}dx$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="497" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{14x^{3} + 2x + 1}{x^{3}}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$14 x - 2 x - 1 2 x 2 + C 14 x - 2 x - 1 2 x 2 + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="498" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$${\int\left( {e^{x} + e^{-x}} \right)}dx$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, solve the initial value problem.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="499" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f^{\prime}(x) = x^{-3},f(1) = 1$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$f ( x ) = - 1 2 x 2 + 3 2 f ( x ) = - 1 2 x 2 + 3 2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="500" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f^{\prime}(x) = \sqrt{x} + x^{2},f(0) = 2$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="501" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f^{\prime}(x) = \cos x + \sec^{2}(x),f\left( \frac{\pi}{4} \right) = 2 + \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$f ( x ) = sin x + tan x + 1 f ( x ) = sin x + tan x + 1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="502" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f^{\prime}(x) = x^{3} - 8x^{2} + 16x + 1,f(0) = 0$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="503" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f^{\prime}(x) = \frac{2}{x^{2}} - \frac{x^{2}}{2},f(1) = 0$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$f ( x ) = - 1 6 x 3 - 2 x + 13 6 f ( x ) = - 1 6 x 3 - 2 x + 13 6$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, find two possible functions $$f$$ given the second- or third-order derivatives.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="504" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f^{''}(x) = x^{2} + 2$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="505" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f^{''}(x) = e^{-x}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>Answers may vary; one possible answer is $$f(x)=e-xf(x)=e-x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="506" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f^{''}(x) = 1 + x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="507" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f \text{'''} (x) = \cos x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>Answers may vary; one possible answer is $$f(x)=-sinxf(x)=-sinx$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="508" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f \text{'''} (x) = 8e^{-2x} - \sin x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="509" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>A car is being driven at a rate of $$40$$ mph when the brakes are applied. The car decelerates at a constant rate of $$10$$ ft/sec2. How long before the car stops?</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$5.8675.867$$ sec</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="510" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>In the preceding problem, calculate how far the car travels in the time it takes to stop.</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="511" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>You are merging onto the freeway, accelerating from rest at a constant rate of $$12$$ ft/sec2. How long does it take you to reach merging speed at $$60$$ mph?</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$7.3337.333$$ sec</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="512" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Based on the previous problem, how far does the car travel to reach merging speed?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="513" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>A car company wants to ensure its newest model can stop in $$8$$ sec when traveling at $$75$$ mph. If we assume constant deceleration, find the value of deceleration that accomplishes this.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$13.7513.75$$ ft/sec2</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="514" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>A car company wants to ensure its newest model can stop in less than $$450$$ ft when traveling at $$60$$ mph. If we assume constant deceleration, find the value of deceleration that accomplishes this.</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, find the antiderivative of the function, assuming $$F(0) = 0.$$</paragraph>
    <exercise number="515" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>[T] $$f(x) = x^{2} + 2$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$F ( x ) = 1 3 x 3 + 2 x F ( x ) = 1 3 x 3 + 2 x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="516" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>[T] $$f(x) = 4x - \sqrt{x}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="517" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>[T] $$f(x) = \sin x + 2x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$F ( x ) = x 2 - cos x + 1 F ( x ) = x 2 - cos x + 1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="518" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>[T] $$f(x) = e^{x}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="519" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>[T] $$f(x) = \frac{1}{\left( {x + 1} \right)^{2}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$F ( x ) = - 1 ( x + 1 ) + 1 F ( x ) = - 1 ( x + 1 ) + 1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="520" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>[T] $$f(x) = e^{-2x} + 3x^{2}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, determine whether the statement is true or false. Either prove it is true or find a counterexample if it is false.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="521" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>If $$f(x)$$ is the antiderivative of $$v(x),$$ then $$2f(x)$$ is the antiderivative of $$2v(x).$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>True</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="522" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>If $$f(x)$$ is the antiderivative of $$v(x),$$ then $$f\left( {2x} \right)$$ is the antiderivative of $$v\left( {2x} \right).$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="523" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>If $$f(x)$$ is the antiderivative of $$v(x),$$ then $$f(x) + 1$$ is the antiderivative of $$v(x) + 1.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>False</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="524" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>If $$f(x)$$ is the antiderivative of $$v(x),$$ then $$\left( {f(x)} \right)^{2}$$ is the antiderivative of $$\left( {v(x)} \right)^{2}.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
  </exercises>
</section>
